<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan bank gets 5.35 bln rupees in operation.</title>
<headline>Pakistan bank gets 5.35 bln rupees in operation.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had accepted 5.35 billion rupees ($133.1 million) in its weekly open market operation in Short-Term Federal Bonds on Wednesday. Following are the results (amount in million rupees):</p>
<p>			Offered	 Accepted	Max cut-off</p>
<p>Outright sales   8,335.50	5,350.50	 17.00 pct</p>
<p>Five-month	   600	     NIL		NIL</p>
<p>Three-month	  NIL	     NIL		NIL</p>
<p>One-month	    NIL	     NIL		NIL</p>
<p>Total		8,935.50	5,350.50</p>
<p>($ = 40.19 Pakistani Rupees)</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
